course: dictionary
lesson: 8241
title: One word, many meanings: rex
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. Rex is a good example. Rex is Latin for "king", and you can see that in names like Tyrannosaurus rex, which means "tyrant lizard king". Tyrannosaurus rex is shortened to T. rex.
explain: How do you know which meaning is right? Look at the clues around it. «Stegosaurus lived about 150 million years ago, so more time separates Stegosaurus from T. rex than separates T. rex from us.» The words dinosaurs and years tell you that T. rex is a giant dinosaur, not a king.
explain: Rex is also a common dog name and a boy's name. «With pets, adults often hide death from children: "Rex went to live on a farm" may mean Rex died or was put down.» The clue is pets: Rex is the name of an animal. Ask yourself what would fit, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: In court cases, rex has a special formal use. "Rex v Smith" means the Crown, the king's side, against Smith, when a king is on the throne. You will only meet this in law, so context and a dictionary will help you.
fact: Rex is Latin for "king", and «regina» is Latin for queen.
fact: «T. rex» is a short name for Tyrannosaurus rex, a huge meat-eating dinosaur.
fact: Rex is a common name for a dog, and it is also a boy's name.
fact: In court cases, "Rex v Smith" means the Crown, the king's side, against Smith, when a king is on the throne.
fact: Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs called theropods, a group that includes T. rex and Velociraptor.
exercise: Rex is Latin for king, and it appears in Tyrannosaurus rex. What does rex mean in Latin? | Dog | Queen | Giant | *King
exercise: «Stegosaurus lived about 150 million years ago, so more time separates Stegosaurus from T. rex than separates T. rex from us.» In this sentence, what is T. rex? | *A huge meat-eating dinosaur | A boy's name | A king's side in court | A common dog name
exercise: Ella's dog is called Rex. What is rex in this sentence? | *A common name for a dog | Scottish for grey and wet | A petrol station | Latin for queen
test: "Rex v Smith" is used in court when a king is on the throne. What does it mean? | Smith is the king and wins | *The Crown, the king's side, against Smith | Smith is a dinosaur | Rex is a judge in the court
test: Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs. Which group do T. rex and Velociraptor belong to? | Plants | Stegosaurus | Fish | *Theropods
exam: Rex is the name of the dog, and rex is also a Latin word. What does rex mean in Latin? | Dinosaur | *King | Dog | Farm
